{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Let their sorrows multiply — those who hasten after</b>: Happy are those who hasten after — and it is from the root of מהר ימהרנה (he will hasten it), that they ally themselves with another people. Only I will not pour their libations, for they are mixed with the blood of their sacrifices, and I will not even mention their names with my mouth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:19.821223371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}